tel 1.0

# The documentation fuel compiles and serves (`fuel compile`, then `fuel serve` at
# http://localhost:8060/), one section each. Every document is read from the Orthant store in
# `.orthant` (.orthant/readme.md), whose live tree is `doc`, where the English is written: an
# edit is in the store once `orthant tag` has stored it. The store's `language` axis has the
# English, `en`, and the French beneath it, `fr`; with no `at`, the `release` axis is read at its
# last value, `main`, what is not yet released. The section `soundness` is the tutorials in
# `modules`, the API overlays in `api`, the glossary, and the section's title in `section.tel`.
store .

section soundness doc/soundness
  metadata section.tel
  overlay api
  glossary glossary.tel

section philosophy doc/philosophy

section standards doc/standards

section roadmap doc/roadmap

section errors doc/errors

# The classpath the fences are compiled against: the test assembly (`./mill test.assembly`,
# which `make test` builds), carrying every JVM component and the fork's standard library.
# Without it the fences are highlighted but not compiled.
classpath out/test/assembly.dest/out.jar

# Components the test assembly leaves out — the WASI backends, the HTTP media bindings and a few
# optional sinks and front-ends — packaged as jars of their own, since fuel reads an API only from
# jars (`make fuelcheck` builds them), so that the API overlays which document them are checked.
classpath out/ambience/wasi/jar.dest/out.jar
classpath out/aviation/wasi/jar.dest/out.jar
classpath out/capricious/wasi/jar.dest/out.jar
classpath out/coaxial/wasi/jar.dest/out.jar
classpath out/galilei/wasi/jar.dest/out.jar
classpath out/telekinesis/wasi/jar.dest/out.jar
classpath out/turbulence/wasi/jar.dest/out.jar
classpath out/telekinesis/forms/jar.dest/out.jar
classpath out/breviloquence/http/jar.dest/out.jar
classpath out/caesura/http/jar.dest/out.jar
classpath out/locomotion/http/jar.dest/out.jar
classpath out/eucalyptus/gcp/jar.dest/out.jar
classpath out/caduceus/resend/jar.dest/out.jar
classpath out/orthodoxy/server/jar.dest/out.jar

# The options Soundness's own code compiles with (settings.scalaOptions in build.mill, less
# the warnings and capture checking a tutorial need not satisfy, and less -Zdiagnostic-givens,
# which renders every given in scope for each failed search and makes a failing fragment slow), with the proscenium predef
# and the umbrella imported, so a fence can start at its first definition.
scalac-option -Zalias-captures
scalac-option -Zgiven-prefixes
scalac-option -Zopaque-mutability
scalac-option -Zpure-iarrays
scalac-option -Zfrozen-pure
scalac-option -Zretains-bounds
scalac-option -Zretains-skolems
scalac-option -Zspreadable-varargs
scalac-option -Zunboxed-pure-types
scalac-option -Zunion-captures
scalac-option -experimental
scalac-option -new-syntax
scalac-option -preview
scalac-option -Yno-flexible-types
scalac-option -Yexplicit-nulls
scalac-option -language:experimental.modularity
scalac-option -language:experimental.dependent
scalac-option -language:experimental.genericNumberLiterals
scalac-option -language:experimental.erasedDefinitions
scalac-option -language:implicitConversions
scalac-option -language:experimental.saferExceptions
scalac-option -language:experimental.subCases
scalac-option -language:experimental.multiSpreads
scalac-option -Yno-predef
scalac-option -Yimports:java.lang,proscenium,soundness

# The tutorials are written as a REPL session (etc/doccheck.py feeds each file's fences to
# flame in order): a fence continues the ones before it, may be a bare expression, and says
# `// does not compile` where it is meant to fail. Fuel compiles each document the same way,
# as one session, with the document's fixture from etc/fixtures compiled first.
session
fixtures etc/fixtures

# The API documentation is one overlay per package beneath doc/soundness/api (the `overlay` of the
# section `soundness`), merged onto the model fuel reads from the classpath above (every
# library is in the test assembly); `imports` is the package a document's or an overlay's
# references resolve through. No `source` directories: Soundness's
# own sources need the fork compiler's syntax, which fuel's session cannot compile, so a
# library's members come from its jar and an overlay is checked against those.
imports soundness

# The words the documents use with a precise meaning, which a term in brackets in prose shows
# the definition of when pointed at (doc/standards/style.md, "Glossary"), are
# doc/soundness/glossary.tel: the `glossary` of the section `soundness`, translated with it.
